course: dictionary
lesson: 12798
title: Electrolytes: salts and charged particles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An electrolyte is a liquid or paste that lets electricity pass through it. It can do this because it contains ions, which are tiny charged particles. «The battery contains an electrolyte that lets electricity flow.» The electrolyte is the middle part that carries the charge.
explain: In your body, electrolytes are salts such as sodium and potassium. They help your muscles and nerves work. «After sweating all afternoon, Sam drank an electrolyte drink.» Sports drinks contain electrolytes to replace the salts you lose when you sweat.
explain: The word has two meanings, one for science and one for health. Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits. A battery is a science clue, while sweating and drinks are health clues.
fact: An electrolyte is a liquid or paste that lets electricity pass through it.
fact: Electrolytes contain ions, which are charged particles.
fact: In the body, electrolytes such as sodium and potassium help your muscles and nerves work.
fact: «Electrolyte drink» means a drink with salts in it, often used after sport or sweating.
fact: «Battery electrolyte» means the liquid or paste inside a battery that carries electricity.
exercise: «The battery has an electrolyte inside it.» What is an electrolyte? | A bright light on a screen | A plastic case that keeps the battery safe | A metal wire that carries power to lights | *A liquid or paste that lets electricity pass through it
exercise: «After sweating all afternoon, Sam drank an electrolyte drink.» Why did he drink it? | To wash out a cut | *To replace salts his body lost | To cool his feet down | To make his voice louder
exercise: «Electrolytes contain ions, which are charged particles.» What are ions? | Loud sounds that echo | Tiny bones in the ear | Small green plants | *Charged particles
test: «Sodium and potassium are electrolytes that your body needs.» What do electrolytes help your body do? | Grow taller in one week | Turn your blood into water | *Help your muscles and nerves work | Make your bones glow in the dark
test: Which sentence uses electrolyte with the science meaning? | The sports drink has electrolytes in it | *The battery's electrolyte lets electricity flow | Sam's electrolyte is his favourite pizza | I went to the electrolyte to buy bread
exam: Ellie says, «Electrolytes are salts in my body and in my drink.» Which meaning is she using, and what does it mean? | *Health meaning: salts that help your muscles and nerves work | Science meaning: a glowing screen | Health meaning: a type of sweet snack | Science meaning: a metal wire carrying power
